<title>USA: Sri Lanka to seek 100,000 T opt-origin wheat - trade.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka to seek 100,000 T opt-origin wheat - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka is expected to seek on February 6 a total of 100,000 tonnes of optional-origin wheat, several U.S. exporters said.  </p>
<p>One U.S. exporter said 50,000 tonnes would be soft wheat and the other 50,000 tonnes would be hard wheat.</p>
<p>&quot;The soft (wheat) would be for February 17-26 (arrival), if it is U.S. and the hard (wheat) would be for March 10-19, if U.S.,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>No other details were available.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
</text>
